WHY THIS DIRECTORY IS LICENSED SEPARATELY

The source code in this repository is MIT-licensed and intended for
unrestricted reuse. This directory is different: it is roughly 254,000 words of
Turkish-language security and software engineering material written for this
project, in a domain where high-quality open Turkish text is scarce. It is
released openly, but attribution is requested when it is reused — including
when it is used as training or evaluation data for machine learning models.

HOW THIS CORPUS WAS PRODUCED (disclosure)

The corpus was authored with large language model assistance and subsequently
curated, quality-scanned, and deduplicated using the tooling in
`uretim_araclari/`. Anyone considering it as training data should factor that
provenance into their own decisions about synthetic-data contamination.

SCOPE

Defensive security education material, written in the OWASP / MITRE ATT&CK
tradition: concept, observable artifact, detection, mitigation. See the
"Security content" section of the repository README for the full framing.
